{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"1cfc08a1ea744f9aaf8c3bea744e598359437c24c270e2865bb8d049df0f3e65","slug":"attribute-completeness","location":"/content/indicators/attribute_completeness.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Attribute Completeness","content_includes_title":false,"numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"thumbnail":"/oqapi-jupyter-book/en/build/attributvollständigk-b9f7649c92effdc06ed287862a398708.png","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"attribute_completeness.md","url":"/oqapi-jupyter-book/en/build/attribute_completene-0319fa35a5b8124fa6790d1908e301ae.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Attribute Completeness indicator shows how detailed and completely additional attributes,\ne.g. street name or speed limit, are mapped in your area of interest. For this indicator, you\nchoose an attribute to investigate from the dropdown menu.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"J99UtYcsoe"}],"key":"eDmdBb3AWG"},{"type":"aside","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/oqapi-jupyter-book/en/build/attributvollständigk-b9f7649c92effdc06ed287862a398708.png","width":250,"key":"zq4txE3GDY","urlSource":"../../abbildungen/attributvollständigkeit.png"}],"key":"mHx1OvIhUS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Depending on the ","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"JwZDL1JsRH"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"topic","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"roGo7tgiy1"}],"key":"oLnuHwCLaw"},{"type":"text","value":", you can choose from a different set of attributes. If you select more\nthan one attribute in a single query, the results are combined, and the result figure shows the\npercentage of all features that have all the selected attributes.","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"ElKM66HNFT"}],"key":"BftZjFQznN"},{"type":"details","children":[{"type":"summary","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defining custom attributes","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"z7orSnfIyR"}],"key":"rxvb5YYnV7"}],"key":"vCb4duhBE3"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also define several attributes, or attributes of your own.","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"CzDS1DQasS"}],"key":"q0FrJNZLNk"}],"key":"RecxbMtl1p"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"KD9cC8zsjG"}],"identifier":"result","label":"Result","html_id":"result","implicit":true,"key":"FH51Z4ASbC"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"You’ll find the results of the query in the result log below.\nThe green, yellow or red banner in the top left shows the attribute completeness level.","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"hLogeH6dk7"}],"key":"eCSmqf0n1I"},{"type":"image","url":"/oqapi-jupyter-book/en/build/attributvollständigk-acc9d98cae44b4fad109ee39e47e4acb.png","width":700,"key":"OjIKknI7ya","urlSource":"../../abbildungen/attributvollständigkeit_frankfurt.png"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Methods and Data","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"QDD9qehzbJ"}],"identifier":"methods-and-data","label":"Methods and Data","html_id":"methods-and-data","implicit":true,"key":"MtmLaoDq9v"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Intrinsic approach","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"TzCJgbj6ln"}],"key":"Fu6zkUS0Ir"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Calculates the percentage of features that hold a given attribute.\nFor point geometries, the total number of features is compared with the number of features that\nhave the selected attributes.\nIf the OSM feature under investigation is a line, the ratio is calculated based on length in km.\nFor polygons, we use the area in km².","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"sTgtBpUjjh"}],"key":"b59W0PvZE3"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are three quality categories:","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"zREUnyd7L4"}],"key":"yv5yUihdLH"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"low completeness < 25%","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"LFIcTvSgs6"}],"key":"G5k1dnnaId"}],"key":"pr5mkhKqf4"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"medium completeness 25% - 75%","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"kIA4QF62dc"}],"key":"pK7Tf2zIdW"}],"key":"ggnu0tcTvf"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"high completeness > 75%","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"eaV2xfVgPb"}],"key":"TByvYwHmja"}],"key":"a3ffTEE6et"}],"key":"yNMxy13DX3"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The thresholds for the quality categories were set by looking at many areas and attributes, and\nshouldn’t be understood as an objective metric.","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"ep1VsZ1QaL"}],"key":"U5qanxya4M"},{"type":"aside","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limitations","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"nHQ82UNdnr"}],"key":"cl4svEX0bI"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some attributes in OpenStreetMap are implied by the presence of other attributes. For example,\nthe speed limit within a living street is typically not explicitly mapped, since it can be\nderived from the road type. These implicit attributes aren’t currently taken into account.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"sVgtwJctar"}],"key":"FddJIKuCq6"}],"key":"WnDH60Xvhf"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The threshold used to assess completeness is the same for every attribute, even though the\nappropriate threshold really depends on the use case.","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"sSihCK0z3x"}],"key":"ISnmkpi0qJ"}],"key":"xUIAmRpF0n"}],"key":"f2XgW1E3w1"}],"key":"wKUsLZIDSP"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"key":"B6bJ8Vvehk"}],"identifier":"examples","label":"Examples","html_id":"examples","implicit":true,"key":"afTo6zQBLR"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the following example, we can see how important it is to choose the right topic. We want to\nfind out the attribute completeness of street names for Frankfurt city centre.","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"FVc3KBLQIQ"}],"key":"Y620C4m4qA"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this figure, we see the result for the topic ","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"ifAnANfb7b"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Roads (all highways)","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"QXO6LHCas2"}],"key":"plPpNhRXVM"},{"type":"text","value":". Just under 40% is a medium\nlevel of completeness, and a surprising result for a large German city. At this point we should\nnotice that something might not be quite right. The topic ","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"sVn3vD1bx4"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Roads (all highways)","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"NxDp5mUHGB"}],"key":"LpEH5Hi8RJ"},{"type":"text","value":" doesn’t just\ninclude roads usable by cars, but every path used for motorised traffic as well as cycleways and\nfootways. Since many cycleways and footways don’t have an explicit name, the query result comes\nout at just under 40%.","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"geuIU1puhE"}],"key":"vEEc9bTBU3"},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/oqapi-jupyter-book/en/build/attributvollständigk-acc9d98cae44b4fad109ee39e47e4acb.png","key":"WB7OvGgeLr","urlSource":"../../abbildungen/attributvollständigkeit_frankfurt.png"}],"key":"oID5o5HjmS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If we’re only interested in the street names of roads used by motorised traffic, we should choose\nthe topic ","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"hx68J8v26S"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Roads (cars)","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"YEWQvzSfYh"}],"key":"t1VuPnfPiv"},{"type":"text","value":" instead. In the next figure, we see that for the same area of interest we\nnow get a high level of completeness.","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"QXvNsa9NxB"}],"key":"UfVU8JG6gI"},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/oqapi-jupyter-book/en/build/attributvollständigk-654fe63839f58e4fb76762ee925db587.png","width":700,"key":"zM1NJm4615","urlSource":"../../abbildungen/attributvollständigkeit_frankfurt_autos.png"}],"key":"sgLd4rV4He"}],"key":"bix8q0kAJu"}],"key":"nH21MB